Below is the full implementation plan for the VS Code agent you described. I have laid it out in the order you would actually build it: architecture decisions first, then the extension skeleton, then each workflow stage with its inputs, outputs, exact commands, failure paths, and code-level design, and finally testing, security, and delivery milestones.

Note: this conversation runs without repository access, so this is a design and implementation plan rather than committed code. Everything below is written so it can be handed directly to whoever builds it (you, or an agent started from a repo-attached surface).

