# 1. What we are building

A VS Code extension that registers a Chat Participant (for example `@jira-dev`). When the user selects it in the Chat view and sends "hi", the participant drives a strict, resumable, multi-stage workflow:

```
hi
 └─► Collect Jira details (key, description, acceptance criteria)
     └─► Collect local repo path ─► switch workspace to that repo
         └─► Collect git strategy (base branch, new branch, commit message)
             └─► git fetch / checkout base / force pull / cut branch
                 └─► Analyze whole codebase ─► produce implementation plan
                     └─► WAIT for user approval of plan
                         └─► Implement changes (agentic edit loop)
                             └─► Clean build ─► fix-loop on compile failures
                                 └─► Start app with dev profile ─► hit /actuator/health
                                     └─► Commit + push with user's message
                                         └─► WAIT: user deploys to dev, confirms
                                             └─► WAIT: user starts test runner locally, gives URL
                                                 └─► Collect kID/password, then clientId/secret
                                                     └─► Open browser, fill logins, go to API, run regression
                                                         └─► Download results
                                                             └─► Generate report (.md or .docx) — ask which
                                                                 └─► WAIT: user validates logs
                                                                     └─► Close session, wipe secrets
Any failure at any stage ──► capture failure context ──► ask user ──► redo from "Analyze & plan"
```

Three things fundamentally shape the design:

1. **Long-lived, interruptible conversation.** The user is asked for input at ~10 distinct points and may take hours between steps (deploying to dev, starting a test runner). The workflow must be a persisted state machine, not a single long function.
2. **Workspace switching reloads the extension host.** `vscode.openFolder` restarts the extension, killing in-memory state. The state machine must survive that and auto-resume.
3. **Browser automation against an unknown test-runner UI.** The login/regression/download selectors cannot be hardcoded; they must be a configurable profile with a recording helper.

